  "answer": "The conditions required for ARP Spoofing include:\n\n1. **Stateless Protocol**: The ARP protocol does not require authentication, allowing devices to incorrectly add or update the MAC address associated with an IP address in their ARP cache [Source 2].\n\n2. **Faster Response**: The attacker must send their ARP reply faster than the legitimate IP address owner\u2019s reply to successfully poison the ARP cache [Source 3].\n\n3. **Local Network Segment**: The attack typically targets devices within the same local network segment, as the attacker sends unverified ARP replies to announce ownership of a particular IP address [Source 3]. \n\nThese conditions facilitate the execution of ARP Spoofing attacks.",
